# dfdreview builds the review page of a leveled design at a review.
# By hand: dfd --box 300x150 --per-row 5 --number docs/flow.dfd -o flow.svg

{Agent at a review}
> options
[1. Open the repository
 to read each file in both versions
 (repo.Open)]
> repository, options
[2. Read the design in both versions
 so each diagram can be drawn before and after
 (design.Read)]
> repository, design
[3. Index the declarations and the changed files
 so each reference finds its code
 (code.Read)]
> design, code index, dfd command
[4. Draw each diagram before, as a diff and after
 so the reviewer sees each change in place
 (draw.Views)]
> options, views, design, code index
[5. Write the page
 with the plan's brief and metaphor, the score cards and the report
 (dfdreview.writePage)]
    > review page
    |Page file|

# type: options = dfdreview.Options
# type: repository = *repo.Repo
# type: design = *design.Design
# type: code index = *code.Index
# type: dfd command = draw.Command
# type: views = []draw.View
